---@meta
-- Generated by rs3-api-types from https://developer.runescape.com/rs/ui/decorative_components/modelgroup.html;
-- regenerate it with ./gradlew generate rather than editing it.

---Model group components contain a set of models meant to be rendered together.
---
---They're meant to work together with Model components, modifying their rendering so they appear in the same scene, and
---also providing a more robust camera model.
---
---Warning: Adding non-model components to model groups is unsupported and will result in a script error.
---
---In the client: A model group can get no camera: AddCamera() without one raises, and ui.ModelCamera cannot be made.
---The client also has UpdateCamera, which the docs do not describe.
---@class ui.ModelGroup : ui.ComponentCollection
---@field activeCameraID integer (Read-only) The index of the currently active camera.
---@field activeCamera ui.ModelCamera? (Read-only) A copy of the currently active camera, or nil if there isn't one.
ui.ModelGroup = {}

---Creates a new model group on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this model group in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.ModelGroup # The newly created model group. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.ModelGroup.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Adds a new defaulted camera, or a previously configured camera to the model group, returning its index.
---@param camera ui.ModelCamera Previously setup camera to add to this model group.
---@return integer
function ui.ModelGroup:AddCamera(camera) end

---Deletes the camera at the provided index if it exists.
---@param cameraIndex integer The index of the camera to be removed.
function ui.ModelGroup:DeleteCamera(cameraIndex) end

---Switches to the camera at the provided index if it exists, starting a transition effect with the specified
---parameters.
---@param cameraIndex integer The index of the camera to switch to.
---@param transition ui.ModelCameraTransition Determines how the visibility for this transition should be calculated over time.
---@param transitionMaskSpriteID integer Numeric ID associated with a sprite for use as a mask for this transition.
---@param transitionDurationMs integer Determines how long this transition lasts for in milliseconds.
---@return boolean # True if the camera exists and a transition was successfully started, false otherwise.
function ui.ModelGroup:SwitchCamera(cameraIndex, transition, transitionMaskSpriteID, transitionDurationMs) end

---Checks if there's a camera present at the specified index.
---@param cameraIndex integer The index of the camera to check.
---@return boolean
function ui.ModelGroup:IsValidCameraID(cameraIndex) end

---Retrieves a copy of the camera present at the specified index.
---@param cameraIndex integer The index of the camera to retrieve.
---@return ui.ModelCamera?
function ui.ModelGroup:GetCamera(cameraIndex) end

---Helper type representing a camera to be used by model group components for rendering.
---
---In the client: There is no table ui.ModelCamera, so a camera cannot be made, and a model group's AddCamera takes one;
---a new model group has none, and its GetCamera and activeCamera give nil.
---@class ui.ModelCamera
---@field clearColour Vector4 Colour used for the background.
---@field useLookAt boolean Determines whether the direction between `position` and `lookAt` is used for the camera, otherwise the camera defaults to looking straight ahead. Note this direction will be modified by `yawPitchRoll`.
---@field transitionRatio number (Read-only) Indicates how far along the current transition is, ranging from `0` (just started) to `1` (finished).
---@field transitionType ui.ModelCameraTransition (Read-only) Type of the current transition, used to determine how the visibility for this camera should be calculated.
---@field transitionMaskSprite integer (Read-only) Numeric ID identifying the sprite to use as a mask for the current transition.
---@field isTransitionInProgress boolean (Read-only) True if there's a transition happening currently.
---@field isTransitionComplete boolean (Read-only) True if there's no transition currently in progress.
---@field sortModelsUsingComponentOrder boolean Controls whether each model contained in this group is rendered separately in the order their components are set to draw, or all together in a single batch. This may be required for cases where there are multiple models with transparency effects present in the same group.
---@field fov number (Read-only) Current field-of-view in degrees for this camera.
---@field position Vector3 (Read-only) Current origin position for this camera.
---@field lookAt Vector3 (Read-only) Current target position for this camera.
---@field yawPitchRoll Vector3 (Read-only) Current rotation in radians to be applied to the camera's direction.
---@field nearPlane number (Read-only) Current minimum distance in world units from the camera before objects are visible.
---@field farPlane number (Read-only) Current maximum distance in world units from the camera before objects are visible.
local ModelCamera = {}

---Starts a transition to this camera using the provided sprite mask.
---
---Warning: Avoid using this directly as camera transitions should be managed by model group components.
---@param transition ui.ModelCameraTransition Determines how the visibility for this transition should be calculated over time.
---@param maskSpriteID integer Numeric ID associated with a sprite for use as a mask for this transition.
---@param durationMs integer Determines how long this transition lasts for in milliseconds.
function ModelCamera:StartTransition(transition, maskSpriteID, durationMs) end

---Resets the transition for this camera, reverting to the initial state.
---
---Warning: Avoid using this directly as camera transitions should be managed by model group components.
function ModelCamera:ClearTransition() end

---Changes the field-of-view for this camera over the specified duration.
---@param fov number Desired field-of-view in degrees. Defaults to `90.0`.
---@param durationMs integer Determines how long this change takes in milliseconds.
function ModelCamera:SetFOV(fov, durationMs) end

---Changes the origin for this camera over the specified duration.
---@param position Vector3 Desired origin for this camera.
---@param durationMs integer Determines how long this change takes in milliseconds.
function ModelCamera:SetPosition(position, durationMs) end

---Changes the target for this camera over the specified duration.
---@param target Vector3
---@param durationMs integer Determines how long this change takes in milliseconds.
function ModelCamera:SetLookAt(target, durationMs) end

---Changes the target for this camera over the specified duration.
---@param yawPitchRoll Vector3 Desired rotations for this camera in radians. If not specified, the camera will point directly at its target as set based on `SetPosition` and `SetLookAt`.
---@param durationMs integer Determines how long this change takes in milliseconds.
function ModelCamera:SetYawPitchRoll(yawPitchRoll, durationMs) end

---Sets the clip planes which control the minimum and maximum distances at which objects are visible for this camera.
---
---Warning: The value used for `far` must be larger than `near`.
---@param near number Minimum distance in world units from the camera before objects are visible.
---@param far number Maximum distance in world units from the camera before objects are visible.
function ModelCamera:SetClipPlanes(near, far) end

---Determines how transitions between multiple model group cameras are handled visually.
---@enum ui.ModelCameraTransition
ui.ModelCameraTransition = {
    ---The transition happens immediately.
    NONE = 0,
    ---The transition source fades out over time.
    FADE = 1,
    ---The transition source fades out as the transition target fades in.
    CROSSFADE = 2,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `ui.ModelCameraTransition.FromID(ui.ModelCameraTransition.NONE)` is `"NONE"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function ui.ModelCameraTransition.FromID(value) end
